---
name: dt-rcf
description: >-
  Root Cause Forensics (RCF) — agentic, multi-entry forensic investigation for Dynatrace.
  Unlike /dt-rca which requires a Davis Problem ID, dt-rcf accepts any forensic anchor:
  Problem ID, service name, time window, trace ID, or error pattern. Dispatches parallel
  forensic workers (dt-obs-problems, dt-obs-tracing, dt-obs-logs, dt-obs-services), builds
  a ranked hypothesis graph with confidence scores, synthesizes via Davis CoPilot, and
  generates a polished MD+PDF forensic report. Use when you need deep RCA, when Davis
  hasn't fired yet, or when the investigation spans multiple services without a clear
  Problem ID anchor.
---

# dt-rcf — Dynatrace Root Cause Forensics

Agentic forensic investigation skill. Accepts any forensic anchor, dispatches parallel
phase workers backed by maintained DQL sub-skills, builds a ranked evidence hypothesis
graph, and produces a complete forensic report (Markdown + PDF).

---

## Usage

```
/dt-rcf P-26012752                                    # Problem ID anchor
/dt-rcf SERVICE:"checkout-api"                        # Service name anchor
/dt-rcf FROM:"2026-05-18T14:00Z" TO:"2026-05-18T15:00Z"  # Time window anchor
/dt-rcf TRACE:"a1b2c3d4e5f6"                         # Trace ID anchor
/dt-rcf ERROR:"connection pool exhausted"             # Error pattern anchor
/dt-rcf P-26012752 -clean                             # Sanitized report
/dt-rcf SERVICE:"order-api" -clean --review           # With reviewer gate
```

## Arguments

- `$ARGUMENTS` — at least one forensic anchor (see types below)
- `-clean` — sanitize all identifying names (same rules as /dt-rca)
- `--review` — add a reviewer subagent quality gate before saving the report

## Sub-Skills Loaded Per Phase

This skill delegates DQL authority to four maintained sub-skills. Do NOT
hardcode DQL that is covered by these references — load the reference; use
its pattern.

| Phase | Sub-skill path |
|---|---|
| W-problems | `~/.agents/skills/dt-obs-problems/SKILL.md` + `references/` |
| W-tracing  | `~/.agents/skills/dt-obs-tracing/SKILL.md` + `references/failure-detection.md`, `references/http-spans.md`, `references/database-spans.md` |
| W-logs     | `~/.agents/skills/dt-obs-logs/SKILL.md` |
| W-services | `~/.agents/skills/dt-obs-services/SKILL.md` + runtime-specific reference (auto-detected) |

**Sanitization, URL format, Mermaid/ASCII diagram rules, and PDF generation:**
These are identical to `/dt-rca`. Read `~/.claude/skills/dt-rca/SKILL.md` sections
"Phase 1.14", "Phase 3", "Phase 4", "PDF DIAGRAM RULES", "MERMAID SYNTAX RULES", and
"DIAGRAM SIZING RULES" — all apply unchanged.

---

## ENTITY MODEL — SMARTSCAPE-NATIVE (NON-NEGOTIABLE)

`classicEntitySelector()` is explicitly deprecated. The four sub-skills use zero
`dt.entity.*` references. dt-rcf MUST use the Smartscape model throughout.

### Span / Log / Event Filtering

```dql
-- Filter spans to a specific service (use Smartscape, NOT dt.entity.service ==)
fetch spans
| filter dt.smartscape.service in [
    smartscapeNodes SERVICE
    | filter id == "{SERVICE_ENTITY_ID}"
    | fields id
]

-- Filter logs to a specific service
fetch logs
| filter dt.smartscape_source.id in [
    smartscapeNodes SERVICE
    | filter id == "{SERVICE_ENTITY_ID}"
    | fields id
]

-- Filter events to a specific host
fetch events
| filter dt.smartscape_source.id in [
    smartscapeNodes HOST
    | filter id == "{HOST_ENTITY_ID}"
    | fields id
]
```

### Entity Name & Metadata Resolution

```dql
-- Resolve service name on spans (preferred over fetch dt.entity.service)
fetch spans
| fieldsAdd service_name = getNodeName(dt.smartscape.service)

-- Resolve host name + hardware on spans
fetch spans
| fieldsAdd host_name = getNodeName(dt.smartscape.host),
            getNodeField(dt.smartscape.host, "bitness"),
            getNodeField(dt.smartscape.host, "additionalSystemInfo")

-- Look up host metadata directly
smartscapeNodes HOST
| filter id == "{HOST_ENTITY_ID}"
| fields name, properties

-- Look up service metadata directly
smartscapeNodes SERVICE
| filter id == "{SERVICE_ENTITY_ID}"
| fields name, properties
```

### Timeseries Metrics (JVM / Process)

```dql
-- Per java.md: group by Smartscape process node, NOT filter by dt.entity.process_group_instance
timeseries gc_count = avg(dt.runtime.jvm.gc.collection_count),
           by: {dt.smartscape.process, dt.process_group.id}
```

### Process Group Metadata (Legacy Gap)

`fetch dt.entity.process_group` has no Smartscape equivalent for `softwareTechnologies`
and `COMMAND_LINE_ARGS` metadata. Use it only for this specific purpose and document
it in the report as a legacy query:

```dql
-- LEGACY — only for softwareTechnologies/command-line metadata (no Smartscape equivalent)
fetch dt.entity.process_group
| filter id == "{PROCESS_GROUP_ID}"
| fieldsAdd entity.name, metadata, tags, softwareTechnologies
```

### Problem Correlation (Dual Model — Transition Period)

Both `affected_entity_ids` (classic) and `smartscape.affected_entity.ids` (Smartscape)
coexist on problem records. Always query BOTH with OR logic:

```dql
fetch logs, from:now() - 2h
| filter dt.smartscape_source.id in [
    fetch dt.davis.problems
    | filter display_id == "{PROBLEM_ID}"
    | filter not(dt.davis.is_duplicate)
    | fields smartscape.affected_entity.ids
] or dt.source_entity in [
    fetch dt.davis.problems
    | filter display_id == "{PROBLEM_ID}"
    | filter not(dt.davis.is_duplicate)
    | fields affected_entity_ids
]
```

### Topology Diagrams

Topology MUST be built from Smartscape relationships, not by stitching `fetch dt.entity.*`
records:

```dql
-- Service dependency topology: services this entity calls and is called by
fetch spans
| filter dt.smartscape.service in [smartscapeNodes SERVICE | filter id == "{ROOT_SERVICE_ID}" | fields id]
| filter span.kind == "client"
| fieldsAdd caller = getNodeName(dt.smartscape.service),
            callee = server.address
| summarize call_count = count(), avg_duration = avg(duration),
            by: {caller, callee}
| sort call_count desc
```

---

## EXECUTION PROTOCOL

### Phase 0a: Multi-Anchor Parser

```
ANCHOR_TYPE + ANCHOR_VALUE:
  P-\d+ pattern (any position)     → PROBLEM
  SERVICE:"<name>" or SERVICE:<name> → SERVICE
  FROM:"<iso>" + TO:"<iso>"         → TIME_WINDOW
  TRACE:"<id>"                      → TRACE
  ERROR:"<pattern>"                 → ERROR_PATTERN

FLAGS:
  -clean    → CLEAN_MODE = true
  --review  → REVIEW_MODE = true

FALLBACK: bare P-\d+ token (no prefix) → PROBLEM
VALIDATION: if no anchor parseable → print usage and exit
```

---

### Phase 0b: Context Bootstrap (Sequential — Orchestrator)

Build the **DispatchContext** that all phase workers receive.

#### If ANCHOR_TYPE == PROBLEM

Run the dt-rca Tier 0 queries (Steps 1.1, 1.1b, 1.1c) from
`~/.claude/skills/dt-rca/SKILL.md`. Extract:

```
PROBLEM_ID            display_id from dt.davis.problems
PROBLEM_START         event.start
PROBLEM_END           event.end (null if still ACTIVE)
ROOT_ENTITY_ID        root_cause_entity_id (classic format: SERVICE-XXXX or PGI-XXXX)
ROOT_ENTITY_NAME      root_cause_entity_name
AFFECTED_ENTITY_IDS[] affected_entity_ids array
ROOT_SERVICE_ID       resolved SERVICE entity ID (from Step 1.1b)
ENTITY_TYPE           SERVICE | PGI | HOST | CUSTOM_DEVICE
INVESTIGATION_STRATEGY error | performance | resource | availability
ENTITY_TAGS[]         tags array
IS_K8S_WORKLOAD       bool (true if k8s tags present)
RUNTIME               java | nodejs | dotnet | python | php | go | unknown
                      (from softwareTechnologies in ENTITY_TAGS or process group)
```

**REQUIRED:** Apply `not(dt.davis.is_duplicate)` on ALL `fetch dt.davis.problems` queries.

DERIVED_TIME_WINDOW:
```
from: PROBLEM_START minus 2h
to:   PROBLEM_END plus 1h (or now() if still ACTIVE)
```

#### If ANCHOR_TYPE == SERVICE

```
Tool: mcp__dynatrace__find_entity_by_name
Input: SERVICE_NAME from ANCHOR_VALUE
Extract: ROOT_SERVICE_ID (SERVICE-XXXX format), ROOT_ENTITY_NAME

DERIVED_TIME_WINDOW: FROM/TO from arguments, or now()-2h to now() if none provided
INVESTIGATION_STRATEGY = "open"
IS_K8S_WORKLOAD = false (unknown — W-tracing will detect from span tags)
RUNTIME = unknown (W-services will detect from span softwareTechnologies)
```

#### If ANCHOR_TYPE == TRACE

```
Tool: mcp__dynatrace__execute_dql
Query:
  fetch spans, from:now()-24h
  | filter trace.id == toUid("{ANCHOR_VALUE}")
  | fieldsAdd service_name = getNodeName(dt.smartscape.service)
  | limit 1
  | fields trace.id, dt.smartscape.service, service_name, start_time

Extract: ROOT_SERVICE_ID from dt.smartscape.service, set DERIVED_TIME_WINDOW ±2h around start_time
INVESTIGATION_STRATEGY = "open"
```

#### If ANCHOR_TYPE == TIME_WINDOW

```
DERIVED_TIME_WINDOW from FROM/TO arguments directly
ROOT_SERVICE_ID = null (W-tracing will surface top error services in window)
INVESTIGATION_STRATEGY = "open"
```

#### If ANCHOR_TYPE == ERROR_PATTERN

```
Tool: mcp__dynatrace__execute_dql
Query:
  fetch logs, from:now()-4h
  | filter matchesPhrase(content, "{ANCHOR_VALUE}")
  | filter loglevel == "ERROR"
  | summarize count = count(), by: {dt.smartscape_source.id}
  | sort count desc
  | limit 1

Extract: top dt.smartscape_source.id → set as ROOT_SERVICE_ID
Query: find service name via smartscapeNodes SERVICE | filter id == ROOT_SERVICE_ID
DERIVED_TIME_WINDOW = now()-4h to now()
INVESTIGATION_STRATEGY = "open"
```

Store everything as **DispatchContext JSON**:

```json
{
  "ANCHOR_TYPE": "...",
  "ANCHOR_VALUE": "...",
  "PROBLEM_ID": "P-XXXX or null",
  "PROBLEM_START": "ISO or null",
  "PROBLEM_END": "ISO or null",
  "ROOT_SERVICE_ID": "SERVICE-XXXX or null",
  "ROOT_ENTITY_ID": "SERVICE/PGI/HOST-XXXX or null",
  "ROOT_ENTITY_NAME": "...",
  "AFFECTED_ENTITY_IDS": [],
  "ENTITY_TYPE": "SERVICE|PGI|HOST|CUSTOM_DEVICE|unknown",
  "INVESTIGATION_STRATEGY": "error|performance|resource|availability|open",
  "ENTITY_TAGS": [],
  "IS_K8S_WORKLOAD": false,
  "RUNTIME": "java|nodejs|dotnet|python|php|go|unknown",
  "DERIVED_TIME_WINDOW": { "from": "ISO", "to": "ISO" },
  "CLEAN_MODE": false,
  "REVIEW_MODE": false
}
```

---

### Phase 1: Parallel Worker Dispatch

**Dispatch in a SINGLE message with multiple Agent calls.** Do NOT run sequentially.

Workers P, T, L, S run concurrently as subagents (`subagent_type: Explore`).
Skip W-problems if ANCHOR_TYPE != PROBLEM.

#### Worker Prompt Template

```
You are a forensic investigation worker for dt-rcf (Dynatrace Root Cause Forensics).

LOAD the sub-skill at {SUB_SKILL_PATH} before writing any DQL.
Also load the reference files listed: {REFERENCE_FILES}
Use ONLY the patterns, field names, and query structures from those references.

ENTITY MODEL — CRITICAL:
- NEVER use dt.entity.service/host == "..." to filter spans or logs.
  Use: filter dt.smartscape.service in [smartscapeNodes SERVICE | filter id == "ID" | fields id]
- NEVER use classicEntitySelector().
- For process group JVM metrics: group by {dt.smartscape.process, dt.process_group.id}
- For entity names: getNodeName(dt.smartscape.service) or getNodeName(dt.smartscape.host)

DISPATCH CONTEXT:
{DISPATCH_CONTEXT_JSON}

QUERIES TO RUN:
{QUERY_INSTRUCTIONS_FOR_THIS_WORKER}

RULES:
- Run all independent queries in parallel (multiple tool calls per message).
- Do NOT return raw rows. Internalize; summarize aggressively.
- Cap your PhaseResult at ~4KB. Top-5 of anything, not top-50.
- If a query fails, retry ONCE with corrected syntax. If it fails again,
  mark as "<gap: reason>" and continue. Do not block on failures.
- Use mcp__dynatrace__* tools. MCP is already authenticated.

RETURN only this PhaseResult shape (JSON). Nothing else.
{PHASE_RESULT_SCHEMA}
```

---

#### W-problems (Skip if ANCHOR_TYPE != PROBLEM)

**Sub-skill:** `~/.agents/skills/dt-obs-problems/SKILL.md`
**References:** `references/problem-correlation.md`, `references/impact-analysis.md`, `references/problem-trending.md`

**Queries to run (in parallel):**

1. Problem details (from dt-rca Step 1.2 adapted with Smartscape dual-model filter)
2. 7-day recurrence history:
   ```dql
   fetch dt.davis.problems, from:now()-7d
   | filter not(dt.davis.is_duplicate)
   | filter root_cause_entity_id == "{ROOT_ENTITY_ID}"
   | fields display_id, event.name, event.status, event.category, event.start, event.end
   | sort event.start desc
   ```
3. Blast radius (from dt-obs-problems > Problem Blast Radius pattern):
   ```dql
   fetch dt.davis.problems, from:now()-90d
   | filter not(dt.davis.is_duplicate)
   | filter display_id == "{PROBLEM_ID}"
   | fieldsAdd affected_count = arraySize(smartscape.affected_entity.ids)
   | fields display_id, affected_count, dt.davis.affected_users_count,
            smartscape.affected_entity.ids, root_cause_entity_name
   ```
4. Deployment correlation (from dt-obs-problems > references/problem-correlation.md)

**PhaseResult shape:**
```json
{
  "problem_summary": { "category": "...", "status": "...", "duration_min": 0 },
  "recurrence_count_7d": 0,
  "prior_problems": [{ "display_id": "...", "start": "...", "category": "..." }],
  "blast_radius": { "entity_count": 0, "user_count": 0 },
  "deployment_in_window": { "found": false, "minutes_before_problem": null, "description": null },
  "gaps": []
}
```

---

#### W-tracing

**Sub-skill:** `~/.agents/skills/dt-obs-tracing/SKILL.md`
**References:** `references/failure-detection.md`, `references/http-spans.md`,
`references/database-spans.md`, `references/sampling-extrapolation.md`

**Queries to run (in parallel):**

1. **Failure reason taxonomy** (dt-obs-tracing > Failure Investigation):
   ```dql
   fetch spans, from:"{DERIVED_TIME_WINDOW.from}"
   | filter start_time >= toTimestamp("{DERIVED_TIME_WINDOW.from}")
       AND start_time <= toTimestamp("{DERIVED_TIME_WINDOW.to}")
   | filter dt.smartscape.service in [
       smartscapeNodes SERVICE | filter id == "{ROOT_SERVICE_ID}" | fields id
   ]
   | filter request.is_failed == true
   | expand dt.failure_detection.results
   | summarize count = count(),
               by: { dt.failure_detection.results[reason] }
   | sort count desc
   ```

2. **Exception types from span.events** (dt-obs-tracing > Exception Analysis):
   ```dql
   fetch spans, from:now()-3d
   | filter start_time >= toTimestamp("{DERIVED_TIME_WINDOW.from}")
       AND start_time <= toTimestamp("{DERIVED_TIME_WINDOW.to}")
   | filter dt.smartscape.service in [
       smartscapeNodes SERVICE | filter id == "{ROOT_SERVICE_ID}" | fields id
   ]
   | filter iAny(span.events[][span_event.name] == "exception")
   | expand span.events
   | fieldsFlatten span.events, fields: { exception.type }
   | summarize count = count(),
               trace = takeAny(record(start_time, trace.id)),
               by: { exception.type }
   | sort count desc
   | limit 10
   ```

3. **Sampling-extrapolated request counts** (dt-obs-tracing > Sampling and Extrapolation):
   ```dql
   fetch spans, from:now()-3d
   | filter start_time >= toTimestamp("{DERIVED_TIME_WINDOW.from}")
       AND start_time <= toTimestamp("{DERIVED_TIME_WINDOW.to}")
   | filter dt.smartscape.service in [
       smartscapeNodes SERVICE | filter id == "{ROOT_SERVICE_ID}" | fields id
   ]
   | filter request.is_root_span == true
   | fieldsAdd sampling.multiplicity = 1 /
       ((power(2, 56) - coalesce(sampling.threshold, 0)) * power(2, -56))
   | fieldsAdd multiplicity = coalesce(sampling.multiplicity, 1)
               * coalesce(aggregation.count, 1)
               * dt.system.sampling_ratio
   | summarize raw_spans = count(), extrapolated_requests = sum(multiplicity),
               failed_spans = countIf(request.is_failed == true),
               by: { bin(start_time, 15m) }
   | sort `bin(start_time, 15m)` asc
   ```

4. **Top failing paths + HTTP status distribution:**
   ```dql
   fetch spans, from:now()-3d
   | filter start_time >= toTimestamp("{DERIVED_TIME_WINDOW.from}")
       AND start_time <= toTimestamp("{DERIVED_TIME_WINDOW.to}")
   | filter dt.smartscape.service in [
       smartscapeNodes SERVICE | filter id == "{ROOT_SERVICE_ID}" | fields id
   ]
   | filter request.is_failed == true and isNotNull(http.response.status_code)
   | summarize count = count(),
               by: { http.response.status_code, endpoint.name }
   | sort count desc
   | limit 15
   ```

5. **Outbound dependency latency** (client spans — detect downstream degradation):
   ```dql
   fetch spans, from:now()-3d
   | filter start_time >= toTimestamp("{DERIVED_TIME_WINDOW.from}")
       AND start_time <= toTimestamp("{DERIVED_TIME_WINDOW.to}")
   | filter dt.smartscape.service in [
       smartscapeNodes SERVICE | filter id == "{ROOT_SERVICE_ID}" | fields id
   ]
   | filter span.kind == "client"
   | summarize call_count = count(), avg_duration_ms = avg(duration)/1000000,
               max_duration_ms = max(duration)/1000000,
               by: { bin(start_time, 15m), span.name }
   | sort `bin(start_time, 15m)` asc
   ```

6. **Span schema discovery** (1 span, full record — find custom request_attribute.* fields):
   ```dql
   fetch spans, from:now()-1h
   | filter dt.smartscape.service in [
       smartscapeNodes SERVICE | filter id == "{ROOT_SERVICE_ID}" | fields id
   ]
   | limit 1
   ```

**PhaseResult shape:**
```json
{
  "failure_reasons": { "http_code": 0, "exception": 0, "grpc_code": 0, "span_status": 0, "custom_rule": 0 },
  "top_exceptions": [{ "type": "...", "count": 0, "sample_trace_id": "..." }],
  "failing_paths": [{ "endpoint": "...", "status_code": 0, "count": 0 }],
  "request_count_raw": 0,
  "request_count_extrapolated": 0,
  "sampling_note": "1 span = ~N requests",
  "outbound_degradation": [{ "span_name": "...", "avg_ms_baseline": 0, "avg_ms_peak": 0 }],
  "custom_request_attributes": [],
  "gaps": []
}
```

---

#### W-logs

**Sub-skill:** `~/.agents/skills/dt-obs-logs/SKILL.md`

**Queries to run (in parallel):**

1. **Error/warn logs with JSON parsing** (dt-obs-logs > Structured / JSON Log Parsing):
   ```dql
   fetch logs, from:now()-3d
   | filter start_time >= toTimestamp("{DERIVED_TIME_WINDOW.from}")
       AND start_time <= toTimestamp("{DERIVED_TIME_WINDOW.to}")
   | filter dt.smartscape_source.id in [
       smartscapeNodes SERVICE | filter id == "{ROOT_SERVICE_ID}" | fields id
   ] or dt.source_entity in [
       smartscapeNodes SERVICE | filter id == "{ROOT_SERVICE_ID}" | fields id
   ]
   | filter in(loglevel, {"ERROR", "WARN"})
   | sort timestamp desc
   | limit 30
   | fields timestamp, content, loglevel, dt.process_group.detected_name
   ```
   Then attempt JSON parse: `| parse content, "JSON:log"` — if it works, extract `log[msg]`, `log[error]`.

2. **Exception / timeout pattern breakdown** (dt-obs-logs > Pattern Analysis):
   ```dql
   fetch logs, from:now()-3d
   | filter start_time >= toTimestamp("{DERIVED_TIME_WINDOW.from}")
       AND start_time <= toTimestamp("{DERIVED_TIME_WINDOW.to}")
   | filter dt.smartscape_source.id in [
       smartscapeNodes SERVICE | filter id == "{ROOT_SERVICE_ID}" | fields id
   ] or dt.source_entity in [
       smartscapeNodes SERVICE | filter id == "{ROOT_SERVICE_ID}" | fields id
   ]
   | filter loglevel == "ERROR"
   | fieldsAdd
       has_exception = if(matchesPhrase(content, "exception") OR matchesPhrase(content, "Exception"), true, else: false),
       has_timeout = if(matchesPhrase(content, "timeout") OR matchesPhrase(content, "timed out"), true, else: false),
       has_oom = if(matchesPhrase(content, "OutOfMemory") OR matchesPhrase(content, "heap space"), true, else: false)
   | summarize
       total_errors = count(),
       exception_count = countIf(has_exception == true),
       timeout_count = countIf(has_timeout == true),
       oom_count = countIf(has_oom == true)
   ```

3. **Log error rate timeseries** (dt-obs-logs > Error Rate Calculation):
   ```dql
   fetch logs, from:now()-3d
   | filter start_time >= toTimestamp("{DERIVED_TIME_WINDOW.from}")
       AND start_time <= toTimestamp("{DERIVED_TIME_WINDOW.to}")
   | filter dt.smartscape_source.id in [
       smartscapeNodes SERVICE | filter id == "{ROOT_SERVICE_ID}" | fields id
   ] or dt.source_entity in [
       smartscapeNodes SERVICE | filter id == "{ROOT_SERVICE_ID}" | fields id
   ]
   | summarize total = count(), errors = countIf(loglevel == "ERROR"),
               by: { bin(timestamp, 15m) }
   | fieldsAdd error_rate_pct = (errors * 100.0) / total
   | sort `bin(timestamp, 15m)` asc
   ```

**PhaseResult shape:**
```json
{
  "top_exceptions": [{ "message": "...", "count": 0 }],
  "timeout_count": 0,
  "oom_count": 0,
  "log_error_rate_trend": [{ "time_bucket": "...", "error_rate_pct": 0 }],
  "log_inflection_time": "ISO or null",
  "raw_samples": [{ "timestamp": "...", "loglevel": "...", "content": "..." }],
  "json_parsed": false,
  "gaps": []
}
```

